# Tutorials. Each story is one tutorial in the docs and one acceptance test.

Story: Your first flight from the launcher
  As a new pilot
  I want to start the sim from one window
  So that I do not need a terminal to fly

  You start the plain T1-S Ranger in the sim alone, with no flight controller. The sim opens
  in its own window, and the launcher shows its output in the LOG screen. When you are done,
  you stop it from the launcher. To fly it, see [[Your first throw]].

  Scenario: Simulator only, without ArduPilot, then stop
    When the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY
    And the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    Then the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the simulator
    And the plane of the started sim is the T1-S Ranger
    And the program is running
    When the pilot stops the program
    Then the program is stopped

Story: Picking what to launch
  As a pilot
  I want to choose what the launcher starts
  So that I fly the plane that I want, where I want

  The LAUNCH screen has a pair of buttons for what to start, a pair for the flight controller,
  a button for each place, and RAY TRACING. The buttons that are lit green are what LAUNCH
  starts. The first line of the LOG screen shows the command that the launcher ran, so you can
  see what it chose. First you fly the VTOL at Cypress, ray traced. Then you start the station
  with the sticks direct.

  Scenario: The VTOL at Cypress, then the station without ArduPilot
    When the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY
    And the place choice is CYPRESS
    And the ray tracing choice is on
    Then the place choice is CYPRESS
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the simulator
    And the plane of the started sim is the T1-S VTOL
    And the place of the started program is Cypress
    And the ray tracing of the started program is on
    When the pilot stops the program
    Then the program is stopped
    When the launch target is GROUND STATION
    And the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    Then the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the ground station
    And the sticks of the started station are direct

Story: Setting up your radio
  As a pilot with a radio
  I want the sim to learn my sticks and switches
  So that the plane does what my hands do

  Plug in your radio, in USB joystick mode. The launcher starts the sim with the radio wizard.
  The wizard asks you to move each stick and switch, and saves what it learns in
  `controls.cfg`. When you close the sim, the CONTROLLERS screen shows the new mapping. For
  the controls of each radio, see [[Controls]].

  Scenario: Set up the controller, then see the mapping
    Given the controls file is missing
    When the pilot sets up the controller
    Then the program in the log is the radio wizard
    When the radio wizard saves controls.cfg and closes
    Then the controls file is mapped
